[]}], "date": 1578567288, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "ffxbld"}, "743": {"changesets": [{"author": "Mozilla Releng Treescript \u003crelease+treescript@mozilla.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "no bug - Bumping Fennec l10n changesets r=release a=l10n-bump DONTBUILD\n\nde -\u003e df74161042ba\ndsb -\u003e 60e629d68254\nfy-NL -\u003e 6afae91b2473\nhi-IN -\u003e 25d10c85f274\nhsb -\u003e c5a74cd7a947\nko -\u003e ce249abe3726\nuk -\u003e b26f15efdd9c\nzh-CN -\u003e e8751a580ef9", "files": ["mobile/locales/l10n-changesets.json"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "dbdf21d91f2cd89455554bea1a1b67cb2f9f829e", "parents": ["12334204b47d6c6242346364a0791168451116ad"], "tags": []}], "date": 1578581819, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "ffxbld"}, "744": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug, mozilla-esr68 repo-update HSTS HPKP blocklist remote-settings tld-suffixes - a=repo-update r=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D59323", "files": ["browser/app/blocklist.xml", "netwerk/dns/effective_tld_names.dat", "security/manager/ssl/StaticHPKPins.h", "security/manager/ssl/nsSTSPreloadList.inc", "services/settings/dumps/blocklists/addons.json", "services/settings/dumps/security-state/onecrl.json"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "3b24696f7db5a8639cd08295a8fa21b5222a39a3", "parents": ["dbdf21d91f2cd89455554bea1a1b67cb2f9f829e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tarek Ziad\u00e9 \u003ctarek@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1478488 - Check for the write-ahead sqlite file in the test. r=valentin, a=test-only\n\nOn windows 10-64 asan, we get a failure on the network io test that\nchecks the sqlite DB is touched. According to the logs, this failure\nhappens because when the test occurs the write happens in the wal\nfile. Adapted the test to also check for that location.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D58908", "files": ["netwerk/test/browser/browser_test_io_activity.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "8e2b542a939b623c3936d6dcd8f19d9e170e69ac", "parents": ["3b24696f7db5a8639cd08295a8fa21b5222a39a3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Petru Lingurar \u003cpetru.lingurar@softvision.ro\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1606820 - Send -1 for current_pwas_count on Android 7.1. r=VladBaicu, a=RyanVM\n\nOn Android 7.1 ShortcutManager#getPinnedShortcuts always returns an empty list\nof pinned shortcuts by the app.\nAlways sending 0 as the number of installed PWAs on Android 7.1 devices would\nskew data so we send the default -1 for this Android version also which is\nknown to be ignored from the telemetry analysis.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D58611", "files": ["mobile/android/base/java/org/mozilla/gecko/telemetry/pingbuilders/TelemetryCorePingBuilder.java"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "9a3cceb94da99e0e9bbe3a5409b28de32523c45e", "parents": ["8e2b542a939b623c3936d6dcd8f19d9e170e69ac"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Petru Lingurar \u003cpetru.lingurar@softvision.ro\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1606820 - Update core-ping documentation for current_pwas_count. r=VladBaicu, a=RyanVM\n\nDepends on D58611\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D58612", "files": ["toolkit/components/telemetry/docs/data/core-ping.rst"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "42d7948c84f3ec52eaa9675d208a266bb584eb56", "parents": ["9a3cceb94da99e0e9bbe3a5409b28de32523c45e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Kaply \u003cmozilla@kaply.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1587492 - Add a new policy to always show the menubar. r=Gijs, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D48724", "files": ["browser/base/content/browser.js", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/Policies.jsm", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/schemas/policies-schema.json", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/tests/browser/browser_policy_display_menu.js", "toolkit/components/utils/JsonSchemaValidator.jsm"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "e805aea014e48f21182f09615f04c0e91539f1e4", "parents": ["42d7948c84f3ec52eaa9675d208a266bb584eb56"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Toshihito Kikuchi \u003ctkikuchi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1601905 - Add quotes for a path including whitespaces in ShellExecuteWithIFile. r=aklotz, a=RyanVM\n\nA fix for Bug 1588975 replaced the call to `LaunchWithIProcess` in\n`nsMIMEInfoWin::LaunchWithFile` with the call to `ShellExecuteWithIFile` to use\n`mozilla::ShellExecuteByExplorer`.  This caused a regression that if a filepath\ncontains whitespaces, we pass it to a target application without quoting it\nwhile the old codepath `ShellExecuteWithIFile` quoted a path accordingly in\n`assembleCmdLine`.\n\nA proposed fix is to quote a path in the same way as `assembleCmdLine` does.\nThis patch also moves `assembleCmdLine` to an exported header so that we can add\na unittest to cover both of `assembleCmdLine` and a new function\n`assembleSingleArgument.  It would be better to refactor these functions in the\nfuture because many lines are duplicated.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D56646", "files": ["toolkit/xre/AssembleCmdLine.h", "toolkit/xre/moz.build", "toolkit/xre/test/gtest/TestAssembleCommandLineWin.cpp", "toolkit/xre/test/gtest/moz.build", "uriloader/exthandler/win/nsMIMEInfoWin.cpp", "xpcom/threads/nsProcessCommon.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "008191a25c1234573e52fc05cde362bc5b8028bb", "parents": ["e805aea014e48f21182f09615f04c0e91539f1e4"], "tags": []}], "date": 1578606715, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null, null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "745": {"changesets": [{"author": "Edmund Wong \u003cewong@pw-wspx.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1338099 - Ensure sourcestamp.txt has a buildid; r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,chmanchester, a=RyanVM\n\nThe $(BUILDID) make variable tries to use either application.ini or\nplatform.ini to fetch the buildid, and if those don't exist then we end\nup with an empty buildid. An error message is displayed, but it doesn't\ncause the make invocation to fail because it happens inside a $(shell).\nInstead we can fetch the buildid similar to the source url, by\ngenerating buildid.h and grabbing the value via awk.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D32518", "files": ["toolkit/mozapps/installer/packager.mk"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "a5bfe5e0d388433fbea5cfcfca462325ce28f089", "parents": ["008191a25c1234573e52fc05cde362bc5b8028bb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Shal \u003cmshal@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1338099 - Export MOZILLA_OFFICIAL in the source build for sourcestamp.txt; r=nalexander, a=RyanVM\n\nMOZ_INCLUDE_SOURCE_INFO is needed for us to write out the MOZ_SOURCE_URL\nin sourcestamp.txt, and MOZ_INCLUDE_SOURCE_INFO is set in configure only\nfor MOZILLA_OFFICIAL=1 builds.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D32519", "files": ["browser/config/mozconfigs/linux64/source"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "e9a7f943da2a4dec1d489685d39b61ecbb26fbec", "parents": ["a5bfe5e0d388433fbea5cfcfca462325ce28f089"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Bryce Seager van Dyk \u003cbvandyk@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1601813 - Parse av01 codec when parsing Widevine manifests. r=dminor, a=RyanVM\n\nThis lets us load Widevine versions that support av1. This doesn't add encrypted\nav1 support, but is one of the steps needed to do so.\n\nThis adds some comments to better clarify the string literals found in the code\nbeing updated.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D56100", "files": ["dom/media/gmp/GMPParent.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "e80192230208035241916274f99327f7d9e665e9", "parents": ["e9a7f943da2a4dec1d489685d39b61ecbb26fbec"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ehsan Akhgari \u003cehsan@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1603902 - Remove a race condition where storage access would get denied when a delayed automatic grant is in progress; r=baku a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D57211", "files": ["dom/base/StorageAccessPermissionRequest.cpp", "dom/base/StorageAccessPermissionRequest.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "c53c8c952ba87b22356511c0bb9ffd16e4cf7b93", "parents": ["e80192230208035241916274f99327f7d9e665e9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Kaply \u003cmozilla@kaply.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1498691 - Allow exceptions for tracking protection in policy. r=mconley, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D57882", "files": ["browser/components/enterprisepolicies/Policies.jsm", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/schemas/policies-schema.json", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/tests/xpcshell/test_permissions.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "e3a7f9d8f84f83d76f8c175efdb46d82cf9bd82e", "parents": ["c53c8c952ba87b22356511c0bb9ffd16e4cf7b93"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Kaply \u003cmozilla@kaply.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1599935 - Make unsupported PDF features a warning. r=bdahl, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D55527", "files": ["browser/extensions/pdfjs/content/PdfjsChromeUtils.jsm"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "737d24fb73b9fc408f39ba6569bed84683925bf3", "parents": ["e3a7f9d8f84f83d76f8c175efdb46d82cf9bd82e"], "tags": []}], "date": 1578608392, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null, null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "746": {"changesets": [{"author": "Csoregi Natalia \u003cncsoregi@mozilla.com\u003e", "br